{"outcome":"built","summary":"I built the display stand. Three full hex bases sit in a triangle: the one already there at (0,0) plus new ones at (0,-1) and (-1,0). A mount spike stands at the corner where all three meet, and the large platform is fitted to it. I then capped every open face (12 solid end caps) and bolted the joints between the bases (3 joint bolts). There are 17 printed parts, about 1,099 g of filament and roughly 1,608 minutes of printing. The final check passed with no rule errors, and the parts don't overlap each other.

I didn't add any display props. The configurator doesn't let props sit on a spike or its platform, and the bases have no covers to put things on. So the build shows the stand itself, with nothing displayed on it.

The BOM notes say to tighten the M6 bolts to about 2 N·m by hand only.","requirements":[{"requirement":"Three bases that meet at one point","status":"met","evidence":"piece:0,0,0, piece:0,-1,0 and piece:-1,0,0 (all full bases) touch each other, bolted together by 3 joint bolts."},{"requirement":"A spike where the three bases meet","status":"met","evidence":"spike:0#-1,0|0,-1|0,0 is a mount spike at the corner shared by all three bases."},{"requirement":"Large platform on the spike, as a display stand","status":"met","evidence":"The large platform (platform-lrg) is fitted to the spike and listed in the BOM as spike-acc-platform-lrg. No prop was placed on it because the configurator doesn't allow props on a spike platform."}]}
